stasis in 4 or more regional lymph nodes   9  nodes POSITIVE out of 17 nodes examined  see Note    NOTE  Some nodal metastases may represent multiple positive matted lymph nodes   but since they were dissected as distinct nodules  they are each classified as a  single positive node for purposes of staging   DISTANT METASTASES  p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  Intraperitoneal metastasis beyond the right lower  quadrant  including pseudomyxoma peritonei   omentum  left perirectal and  anterior cul de sac  bilateral ovaries  endometrium  see separately submitted  specimens A  E  F  and G  and prior specimen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     MISMATCH REPAIR PROTEIN EXPRESSION  Immunohistochemical stains for DNA mismatch  repair proteins show preserved expression of all proteins  h REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   h REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   h REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    and h REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       COMMENT  The majority of the tumor has the appearance of a poorly  differentiated adenocarcinoma  consisting of infiltrating single cells and small  clusters or cords of cells with plasmacytoid and signet ring cell morphology   extensively and circumferentially involving the full thickness of the appendix   Within the wall of the appendix  there are occasional rounded clusters of tumor  that contain goblet cells and are reminiscent of goblet cell carcinoid  although  they exhibit a higher degree of cytologic atypia than is typically seen in  goblet cell carcinoid  Although a truly low grade component is not definitively  present  these findings suggest that the tumor arose from a goblet cell  carcinoid that is now essentially completely overrun  Thus  the tumor is judged  most consistent with adenocarcinoma ex goblet cell carcinoid  poorly  differentiated adenocarcinoma type  Group C  according to one proposed  classification for appendiceal carcinomas  Tang LH et al  Am J Surg Pathol  32 10   REMOVED_CASE_ID  43   REMOVED_CASE_ID       D  UTERUS  HYSTERECTOMY   Inactive endometrium   There is no eviden