ectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm area ellipse of skin on the anterior margin  which is oriented with a long stitch right lateral  and a short stitch superior  and contains an unremarkable nipple and areola  The skin surface also extends for a distance of 3cm inferomedial to the areola  A 3cm long linear groove consistent with a prior excision is present on the skin running a distance of 2 5cm along the medial lateral edge of the ellipse  0 1cm from the edge of the skin  1cm from the skin margin in the inferomedial quadrant of the breast is a defect in the anterior margin which measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and shows granularity of the surrounding soft tissue  A cavitary area  consistent with prior excision cavity is seen through this defect  The remaining anterior margin consists of unremarkable yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  The posterior margin consists of smooth fascia overlying fibroadipose tissue  however  there is a 1 x 1cm defect in the posterior margin in the inferomedial quadrant  which communicates with the previously mentioned cavity  The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm cavity lined by granular yellow pink tissue and with fat necrosis in a patchy distribution within the surrounding breast parenchyma  The biopsy cavity extends to the aforementioned defects in the anterior and posterior margins  The cavity itself extends to approximately 4cm from the nipple  Multiple metal surgical clips are identified in the wall of the cavity  Additional nodules of fat necrosis and focal hemorrhage extend laterally and superiorly for approximately 3cm from the cavity  A firm  punctate red brown 0 2cm lesion with radiating fat necrosis and fibrous tissue over an area of roughly 1 5cm is present 2 5cm superior to the biopsy cavity  The remaining breast parenchyma consists primarily of adipose breast tissue with no focal lesions identifi