Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  19 MAY 98 at 12 20 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVE MARGIN    EXCISION  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO ONE LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  LOWER LEVEL 2   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO ONE LYMPH NODE WITH FOCAL EXTRANODAL SOFT TISSUE EXTENSION  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL 15 LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 98 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm breast fragment with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm firm and gritty  stellate  white mass which grossly abuts the superficial margin  The tumor is focally less than 0 1cm from the lateral margin  focally 0 3cm from the superior margin  and at least 0 4cm from the deep margin  Representative section of the tumor abutting the superficial margin is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tumor is submitted in cassettes B through D  with the superficial  deep  and superior margins demonstrated in B  deep margin demonstrated in C  and lateral margin in D   The superior aspect is overinked green  and the deep aspect overinked blue   A second 0 3cm firm  well circumscribed nodule is located medial to the mass  and is grossly cleared of all surrounding margins  submitted in cassette E  Representative section of uninvolved dense breast tissue is in cassette F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in 5 parts  labeled  add deep margin L breast  is an irregular 3 7x 2 7x 1 0cm fragment of primarily fatty unremarkable tissue  most of which is submitted in cassettes G and H  Labeled  final shave L breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 