Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 AUG 96 at 11 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  SLIDE B AND F   WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I II III   WITH A SINGLE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PAPILLARY AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  LOW GRADE  FORMING A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS  PRESENT AT OR LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  NOTE  Accurate assessment of the size of the invasive carcinoma is difficult in the setting of architectural distortion which is associated with the marked periductal fibrosis  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of invasive carcinoma  Dr  Koerner has reviewed selected slides and agrees with the interpretation  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Multiple levels examined  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 96 at 15 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma cells are not identified in the sections stained for hormone receptor protein  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  tan  well circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm mass with focal pink tan tissue area at nearest inked margin  A portion is frozen as FX 1 and submitted in cassette A  The remainder is totally submitted in cassette B through J  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  AWAIT PERMANENTS TO RULE OUT INVASION  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
