Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Skin biopsy  other than cyst tag debrid repair  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ROGER L CHRISTIAN M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Jian Shen  M D   Ph D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST  SKIN TAGS  EXCISION   Acrochordons   RIGHT BREAST EXCISION  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR THREE CLIPS   Tumor bed with fibrosis  chronic inflammation  and hemosiderin deposition  2  cm  present in the area of the three clips  see note    Calcifications are associated with benign epithelium   Skin with no tumor seen   NOTE  The patient presented with a 2 0cm palpable carcinoma by ultrasound and  mammogram  correlating with a 1 9cm area of MRI enhancement  After treatment  with four cycles of cisplatin  ultrasound and mammography showed a marked  decrease in the size of the carcinoma and there was a complete resolution of  prior MRI enhancement   Grossly a 2 0cm fibrotic area is present correlating with the tumor bed  No  residual carcinoma is identified after complete microscopic examination of the  tumor bed  including margins  This would be considered a complete pathologic  response or a Miller Payne score of 5   RIGHT BREAST  SUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION   Breast parenchyma with no tumor present   RIGHT BREAST  INFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION   Breast parenchyma with no tumor present   AXILLARY CONTENTS   Five  5  lymph nodes with no tumor present  see note    NOTE  The patient presented with multiple palpable lymph nodes  the largest  measuring 2 4cm by MRI  and metastatic tumor was documented by FNA  By report   there was marked decrease in size after neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Areas of  fibrosis are present in all five lymph nodes consistent with treated tumor  No  residual carcinoma is seen  This is a complete pathologic response in the  lymph nodes   Because only five 