Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Consult slide s   Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MONICA M BERTAGNOLLI M D   CASE  BS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   PATIENT  M  JOHNSON  Resident  BRIAN S  CHANG  M D   PH D   Pathologist  SUSAN LESTER  M D   PH D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   CONSULT SLIDES FROM BETH ISRAEL DEACONESS MEDICAL CENTER  BOSTON  MA   LEFT BREAST  12 00  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A MASS  04  REMOVED_CASE_ID   11 03 04    UNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA  see note below    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results  not  reviewed    Keratin Positive  Vimentin Positive  Actin Focally positive   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Negative  Desmin Negative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Negative  LEFT BREAST  TWO EXCISIONS  04  REMOVED_CASE_ID   11 24 04    LEFT INFRACLAVICULAR MASS   UNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA  1 4cm  invading in fibroadipose tissue  adjacent to atrophic skeletal muscle  see note    The tumor is present at the margins   Biopsy site changes are present   Only rare ducts are present  consistent with breast parenchyma   Note  A paraffin block was previously sent for consultation to Dr  C  D   Fletcher and his consultation letter follows  previously reported as  BS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      I agree with you that this is a difficult lesion  While  at first glance   areas of the lesion show scarring and xanthogranulomatous inflammation   presumably due to the prior therapy  nevertheless  there is a subtle but  undoubtedly atypical spindle cell proliferation  in areas dissecting through  the fat and in other areas having a remarkable pseudovascular growth pattern   Some parts of the lesion have a prominent collagenous stroma and the lesional  margin is diffusely infiltrative  In our hands  there is no  immunohistochemical evidence of specific differentiation   stains for  pan keratin  keratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   EMA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are all negative  In these  circumstances  I would regard this as an unclassified spindle cell sarcoma   morphologically low grade  likely radiation associated  As you know  a high  proportion of post radiation sarcomas are otherwise unclassifiable  In the  experience of our sarcoma clinic  tumours of this type often pose considerable  problems in terms of local control  perhaps due to a radiation field effect    rather than being associated with a high risk of metastasis  In these  circumstances  wide excision would be advisable    Dr  Fletcher also reviewed the additional HE slides received and his diagnosis  is unchanged   Additional immunoperoxidase studies were performed at Beth Israel Deaconess  Medical Center with the following results  not reviewed    PANK MNF 116 Positive  Keratin cocktail Positive   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Negative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Negative  Factor VIII Negative  Desmin Negative  Actin Negative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Negative  Estrogen receptor Negative  Progesterone receptor Negative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu Negative  LEFT INFERIOR LATERAL INFRACLAVICULAR MASS   UNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA   Tumor is present at the margin   Note  The specimen was received in multiple fragments  in aggregate  1 8cm   CLINICAL DATA   History  History of breast cancer  new left mass   Operation  Not provided   Operative Findings  None given   Clinical Diagnosis  None given   TISSUE SUBMITTED   Consult slides   GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received from Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center  Pathology Department   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   are sixteen  16  glass slides   One  1  slide is labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sublabeled  A LEVEL 1   corresponding  to a left breast  12 00  7cm from nipple  core biopsy for a mass  1 6 x REMOVED_DATE  cm  performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report  bearing the patient s name   Fifteen  15  slides are labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and