 in the background of the case  Dr  Koerner has reviewed  the case and concurs with the above interpretation     BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN CEPHALAD   EXCISION   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT IN 3 OF 4 BLOCKS     BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN CAUDAD   EXCISION   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  BOTH LOW AND HIGHER GRADE PATTERNS  PRESENT IN 5 OF 5  BLOCKS     NOTE  E cadherin stain shows rare cells weakly positive in the higher grade  DCIS  consistent with the loss of E cadherin pattern noted in specimen A     BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT IN 2 OF 4 BLOCKS     BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT IN 4 OF 4 BLOCKS   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   SEE NOTE     NOTE  To evaluate for invasive carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  calponin  smooth muscle myosin heavy chain  p63  and cytokeratin were examined   the findings support the above diagnosis       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 5 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh  labeled  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  piece of fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization guidewire  oriented as  follows  Short   anterior  long   lateral  bowtie   cephalad  The long axis  of the specimen runs from medial to lateral  The anterior margin of the  specimen is inked blue  the posterior margin black  the superior margin green   and the inferior margin yellow  It contains a well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  soft hemorrhagic nodule  located 0 1cm from the superior margin  2 0cm from  the inferior margin  1 2cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior  margin  2 5cm from the medial tip  and 1 8cm from the lateral tip  There is  abundant surrounding tan white fibrous tissue adjacent to the nodule  The  remainder of the specimen consists predominantly of unremarkable fibroadipose  tissue  with admixed scant tan white fibrous tissue and focal hemorrhage  No  metal clips are identified  Representative sections of the specimen are  submitted as follows     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule  entirely submitted  with bisected cross sections of the  specimen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Bisected cross section medial to nodule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Bisected cross section lateral to nodule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue medial to nodule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue lateral to nodule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial tip  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral tip  en face     Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final cephalad   is an unoriented  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose and tan white fibrous tissue with  cautery  which is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final caudad   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue and admixed tan white fibrous  tissue  with cautery  which is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final medial   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with admixed tan white fibrous  tissue and cautery  which is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final lateral   is an unoriented  2 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with admixed tan white fibrous  tissue  with focal hemorrhage  which is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday  REMOVED_MONTH 29   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08 29 51AM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and c