Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ESTHER RHEI M D   CASE  BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Elgida Radoncipi  M D   Pathologist  Alessandra F Nascimento  M D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  EXCISION   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU and columnar cell change   Biopsy site changes   CLINICAL DATA   History  41 year old premenopausal female with a family history of breast  cancer in her mother  62   Patient noted a right breast mass  REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrated an area of focal asymmetry  4 3cm by ultrasound   7 8 09 core biopsy revealed fibrous breast tissue without features of a mass  forming lesion  The patient prefers excision   Operation  excision of a right breast mass   Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast mass   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Right breast tissue  Short suture superior  long suture lateral   whipstitch on deep margin   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   and  right breast tissue short suture superior long lateral whip stitch deep  margin   and consists of a tan yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast  tissue  4 0cm medial to lateral  3 0cm superior to inferior  and 1 5cm  anterior to posterior  with a short suture designating the superior margin   long suture designating the lateral margin  and whip stitch designating the  posterior deep margin  There is no needle localization wire in place and the  specimen is not received with a radiograph  The specimen is inked per  pathology protocol  superior red  inferior green  medial orange  lateral  yellow  anterior blue  and posterior black  and serially sectioned from medial  to lateral  The cut surface consists primarily of dense white fibrous tissue  constituting greater than 95  of the breast parenchyma  No discrete lesions   previous