Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 37 CLINICAL DATA  29 year old female with infiltrative and intraductal carcinoma on outside biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT IN THE TISSUE SURROUNDING THE BIOPSY SITE  THE RESECTION MARGINS ARE FREE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO  CRIBIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT IN THE TISSUE SURROUNDING THE BIOPSY CAVITY ON 2 OF 8 SECTIONS  THE RESECTION MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  FAT NECROSIS  LIPID LADEN MACROPHAGES  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL GRANULOMAS  CONSISTENT WITH SITE OF PREVIOUS SURGERY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The metastatic carcinoma measures less than 0 2cm and is confined to the lymph node  no extracapsular tumor is seen  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  Note  Immunoperoxidase stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  02 AUG 95 at 16 04 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm breast and axillary tail with an overlying ellipse of skin  REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  There is a 4 0cm line about 3 5cm from the nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm cavity is present about 1 0cm from the deep inked margin and 1 5cm from the overlying skin  The wall of the cavity is hard  tan and nodular in several areas  but otherwise smooth  The breast parenchyma around the biopsy cavity is rubbery  tan and slightly nodular  The rest of breast parenchyma is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A  closest margin to biopsy cavity on the deep inked margin  B E  representative sections of wall of the biopsy cavity  F H  representative sections of fibrous area around the biopsy cavity  I L  lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional inferior margin   are two pieces of breast tissue  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and the smaller measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections of breast parenchyma from larger portion are submitted in cassettes M and N  and a representative section from the smallest portion is submitted in cassette O  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  PART B  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   report_end  , not_surgery.
