 of attached tan yellow adipose  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right breast   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the axillary tail  The overlying tan brown skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 3 0cm in length curvilinear  well healed scar present approximately between 5 and 7 o clock position  0 5cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior margin   blue and posterior margin   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial  lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cavity with a tan brown  shaggy lining  located beneath the curvilinear scar and containing tan brown hemorrhagic material  The breast parenchyma surrounding the cavity shows foci of fat necrosis  The cavity is located 1 4cm from the anterior and 4 5cm from the posterior inked margins  The rest of the breast parenchyma in the inner and outer quadrants shows diffuse  tan white  rubbery  nodular fibrous tissue  In addition  0 4cm from the unremarkable nipple and 0 6cm from the curvilinear scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan yellow papule  Finally  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated at the level of the sutured axillary tail  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cavity  beneath the scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the nodular breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the nodular breast parenchyma  lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Another representative section of the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tan yellow papule near the nipple areo