 invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ focally extends to less than 0 1cm from the superior and lateral margins  to 0 1cm from the anterior and superoposterior margins  and to 0 15cm from the inferoposterior and posterior margins  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  although the amount of tumor may be insufficient for receptor studies  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  1  A FEW SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  A cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE stain on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is positive in a proliferative focus  consistent with usual ductal hyperplasia  The few in situ tumor cells remaining on the immunostained slide are negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE Multiple levels examined  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  1  A FEW SMALL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  A MINUTE FOCUS OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA CANNOT BE ENTIRELY EXCLUDED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE stains on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  confirm that larger  proliferative foci represent usual ductal hyperplasia  A small irregular focus of cells on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  may be distorted due to artifact  but focal stromal invasion cannot be entirely excluded and the focus is too small for further studies  Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy short stitch superior  long stitch equals lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan pink fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating superior and a long black stitch designating the lateral margin  Th