Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  A   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  45   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  CRP 8  NEUROPATHY CNTR PYS  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 17 08  Results To   Tracey Alexander Cho MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     SKIN  STANDARD DISTAL LEG   PUNCH BIOPSY   Qualitative microscopic examination of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  5 immuno labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   revealed marked reduction of epidermal and dermal innervation  consistent with  axonopathy of small cutaneous sensory axons  Intra axonal swellings were  prominent in remaining axons  the presence of excess axonal swellings is  associated with small fiber polyneuropathy     Morphometric quantitation of epidermal nerve endings yielded a density of 113  neurites mm2 of skin surface area  at less than the 1st centile based on our  laboratory s age  sex  and race adjusted normative data series  Values at or  below the 5th centile are considered diagnostic for a small fiber axonopathy   This density can be monitored with future biopsies to evaluate disease  progression or the effects of therapy     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U  S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision          Electronically Signed Out By Anne Louise Oaklander MD  PhD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       CLINICAL HISTORY  Question of small fiber polyneuropathy     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  SKIN BIOPSY  Nerve Injury Unit     GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in the NIU lab in Zamboni s fixative   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  and designated from site right standard distal leg  is a 0 3cm  circular skin punch excised to a depth of approximately 0 2cm  The specimen is  designated skin biopsy number  REMOVED_CASE_ID          PART   SKIN BIOPSY  Nerve Injury Unit        report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
