urface over inked blue and the posterior surface over inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal the absence of gross lesions suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  from lateral to medial aspects  with A the most lateral  J the most medial  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a 8 x 6 x 2cm aggregate of unremarkable adipose tissue  A lymph node dissection is performed with lymph nodes submitted in K through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of adipose tissue with one lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette Q  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST EXCISION   NO INVASIVE CARCINOMA GROSSLY IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  2   EXCISION   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
