ochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is an 8 x 5 x 3cm portion of breast tissue with a guide wire  A short suture designates the superior margin and a long stitch designates the lateral margin  The entire surface is inked black  with the anterior aspect overinked red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a hard  white nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  in the inferomedial portion of the specimen  coming within 0 3cm of the closest margin  inferior   No frozen section was done  The nodule in relation to closest inferior and anterior margins is submitted in cassettes A B  The remainder of the nodule in relation to inferior margin is submitted in cassette C  The remaining margins are grossly uninvolved  Sectioning through the parenchyma reveals predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue interspersed with a minute amount of delicate  fibrous tissue  Representative section of the sparse fibrous tissue is submitted in cassette D in relation to the anterior margin  and in cassette E in relation to the superior margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node  rule out met  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node 