 conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Resident Review by Deborah A Dillon M D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  6 24 05   DR  DEBORAH DILLON  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for INVASIVE carcinoma  outside block    Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   POSITIVE  3    Note  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen  and progesterone receptors   Interpretation   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only  a portion of the membrane is positive   Positive  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10   of tumor cells   Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
