Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  status post chemotherapy  inflammatory cancer of breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Carcinoma extensively involves lymphatics throughout the breast parenchyma and subareolar tissue  The inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  3  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 2 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  In addition to the 3 lymph nodes  two nodules of carcinoma devoid of lymphoid tissue are present  These nodules may represent carcinoma completely replacing lymph nodes or carcinoma infiltrating the adipose tissue  Extensive involvement of lymphatics in the area of the lymph nodes is present  Diagnosis by  Deborah S  Fleischhacker  MD ScD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 1 610 gram simple mastectomy specimen  The breast parenchyma measures 26 x REMOVED_DATE x 6cm with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm axillary region  The attached REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm ellipse of skin has a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 4cm areola and a 1 x 1cm centrally placed nipple located 3cm from the inferior resection margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm  tan  fibrotic area with focal  yellow to green necrotic nodules measuring 0 2cm in greatest dimension  This area is located 2 5cm from the inferior margin  which is the closest margin  5 5cm from the deep margin of resection  and 2 2cm from the overlying nipple  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of adipose tissue and firm  fibrotic strands of white breast parenchyma  The axillary region contains numerous firm lymph nodes measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension  SECTION CODE  A  Nipple  en face  B  Nipple and tumor  transverse  C E  Representative sections of tumor  F  Tumor and inferior resection margin  closest margin  G  Deep resection margin  H  Superior resection margin  I  Medial resection margin  J  Lateral resection margin  K  Firm area 3cm medial to tumor mass  L  Normal breast parenchyma  M  Biopsy site  N U  Lymph nodes  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , not_surgery.
