brous tissue  comprising approximately 20 30  of the specimen  The fibrous areas are located predominantly in the portion of the tissue anterior to the implant  No area consistent with the biopsy cavity is grossly identified  Representative sections of the most fibrous areas are submitted in A L  with the fibrous tissue anterior to the implant in A I  tissue with deep margin in J K  and a section of the nipple in L  The area presumed to be closest to the axilla is examined for lymph nodes  however none are identified  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast implant  is a deflated  disc shaped portion of material measuring 9 5cm in diameter  There is a letter  P  imprinted on one surface  This specimen is photographed and submitted for gross diagnosis only  Dr  Fan has confirmed the diagnosis  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  partially covered by a membranous fascial layer  Serial sectioning reveals unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  without nodules  masses or calcifications  Representative sections are submitted in M and N  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   IMPLANT REMOVAL , not_surgery.
