Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  None provided  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADJACENT TO AND SLIGHTLY BEYOND THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND  0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  UNEQUIVOCAL EVIDENCE OF INVASION IS NOT SEEN  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  CALCIFIED FIBROADENOMAS  5  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH REMOTE BIOPSY SITE AND PRIOR IRRADIATION  NOTE  A small  irregular focus of carcinoma is noted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although most of the tumor in this focus is associated with myoepithelial cells  a few very tiny clusters do not show clearly evident myoepithelial cells in immunostained sections  Given the overall morphologic appearance  however  these are favored to represent distorted in situ carcinoma with myoepithelial cell attenuation  although the possibility of very minute microinvasion cannot be entirely excluded  Immunostains for calponin  SM MHC  and p63 were examined on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10 5cm brown skin with a centrally located 1 2cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen has an undesignated stitch at one aspect  which is presumed to be 12 o clock  There are multiple brown macules on the epidermal surface ranging from 0 2cm to 0 5cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm cavity containing brown fluid  consistent with a previous biopsy cavity  which is located in the central to outer aspect  The biopsy cavity extends to within 2 2cm of the nearest posterior margin and 1 7cm of the skin surface  Identified 1 0cm inferior to the biopsy cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm calcified gray white nodule  which extends to within 1 7cm of the posterior margin and 3 2cm of the anterior margin  Also identified at the lateral aspect of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm gray white nodule which measures 3 2cm from the biopsy cavity and 3 5cm from the aforementioned indurated mass  This third mass measures 0 6cm to the posterior margin and 1 5cm to the anterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  The presumed lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated and lymph nodes are not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the biopsy cavity  with sections to the nearest posterior margin in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity to the calcified nodule  after decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the calcified nodule to the posterior margin  after decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue between the biopsy cavity and the third nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire third nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from all nodules  Final Diagno