 description  the tumor mass was described as being present in the  left outer quadrant  this should read lower outer quadrant   Immunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for invasive  carcinoma in the breast  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and metastatic carcinoma to a lymph node   block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu WEAKLY FOCALLY POSITIVE  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and  progesterone receptors in the breast   Prior to treatment  the carcinoma was reported to be negative for ER and PR   The pre treatment carcinoma was variably positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu and a FISH study  showed amplification with a ratio of REMOVED_DATE The post treatment findings are the  same  There is very focal weak to moderate immunoreactivity for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu in  both the breast and the lymph node   Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , not_surgery.
