this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens  Labeled  Left breast   is an oriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with contiguous axillary lymph node dissection and an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse  containing an unremarkable 0 9cm medial nipple  and two well healed vertical scars  2 1cm long each  REMOVED_DATE and 9 8cm lateral to the nipple  The deep resection margin of the specimen is a smooth  fascial plane  Sectioning reveals a 1 7cm in greatest diameter  blood filled cavity  1 0cm below the medial biopsy scar  1 1cm from the inferior resection margin  and 3 2cm from the deep resection margin  The cavity is surrounded by scant yellow fat necrosis  A 0 8cm blood filled cavity is located 1 2cm beneath the lateral scar  1 6cm from the deep resection margin  a 2 2cm from the inferior resection margin  The cavity is surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of tan  rubbery  well circumscribed tissue medially  which comes to within 0 7cm from the deep resection margin  Threecm superior medially to the medial biopsy cavity is a 0 7cm firm  gritty  tan pink lesion  2 1cm from the deep resection margin  closest   The remaining adipose tissue is unremarkable  The attached axillary lymph node dissection contains nineteen lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 1cm in greatest diameter  Labeled  Additional axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  containing a 1 3cm firm  tan nodule  and a 0 2cm soft nodule  SECTION CODE  A D  medial biopsy cavity  E  inferior margin  medial biopsy cavity  F G  lateral biopsy cavity  H  deep resection margin of lateral biopsy cavity  I  medial thickening of lateral biopsy cavity  J K  small nodule  entirely  L  nipple and medial scar  M  lateral scar  N S  contiguous axillary nodes  entirely  T  separately submitted additional axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Martha Elizabeth Meaney  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
