ollicular dendritic cell aggregates  A stain for Ki67 shows an appropriately high level of staining within reactive follicles  There is no staining of lymphoid cells with an antibody to cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In situ hybridization for kappa and lambda immunoglobulin light chains highlights polytypic plasma cells  The overall morphologic and immunophenotypic findings support a reactive process for the lymph node enlargement  but the specific etiology is uncertain  The presence of reactive follicular hyperplasia with increased monocytoid B cells and clusters of epithelioid histiocytes at least focally raises the possibility of toxoplasma associated lymphadenitis  Correlation with serologic studies may be informative  This immunoperoxidase test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  area  1  10 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled   area  2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL IMMUNOHISTOCHEM