 MRI  Grossly  two  masses were seen  measuring 1 4cm and 0 8cm  Histologically  these  correspond to a 1 9cm focus of residual carcinoma and a 0 3cm focus of  residual carcinoma  both foci present in association with biopsy site changes  and focal stromal changes suggestive of treatment response  Tissue sampled  between the two grossly evident lesions also shows invasive carcinoma   Cellularity is widely variable  with both cellular areas and widely scattered  small foci  Findings are compatible with a grade 2 or 3 response in the  Miller Payne system   CLINICAL DATA   History  Status post neo adjuvant chemotherapy Xeloda on protocol  status post  4 4 positive   Operation  Left breast tissue localized partial mastectomy   Operative Findings  None given   Clinical Diagnosis  Preop  Left breast cancer  Postop  Left breast cancer   ORGANS TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast wire localized partial mastectomy to mammo   B 2  Left breast lateral posterior margin   short equals superior  long equals  lateral   C 3  Left axillary content   RADIOLOGY  Calcifications and clip  known cancer and second mass with clip   second known cancer  all in specimen  C  Denison  MD  GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  in containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   patient s name and medical record number   Part A   Left wire localized partial mastectomy to mammo   consists of an  oriented partial mastectomy specimen  9 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm  50 grams  oriented by  two sutures as follows  Long   lateral  short   superior  The specimen is  inked for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue   superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  Three  localization wires enter the specimen  Needle  1 enters laterally and extends  medially  Needle  2 enters medially  slightly more anteriorly  and extends  laterally  Needle  3 enters medially  slightly more posteriorly  and extends  medially posteriorly inferiorly  The specimen is sectioned from medial to  lateral in 13 slices  There is a tan yellow biopsy cavity  0 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm    with surrounding firm  white fibrous tissue  1 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm    This mass is  adjacent to needle 2 and 3  located in slices 2 through 5  and designated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The mass is located 1 4cm from the deep margin  1 4cm from the anterior  margin  1 2cm from the superior margin  1 6cm from the inferior margin  REMOVED_DATE  cm from the medial margin  and approximately 4cm to the lateral margin   Lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is a second biopsy site with surrounding white fibrous tissue   0 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm   adjacent to needle 1  This mass is designated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and is  located 0 5cm from the inferior margin  0 7cm from the anterior margin  REMOVED_DATE  cm from the superior margin  2 8cm to the deep margin  1 5cm to the lateral  margin  and approximately 6 5cm from the medial margin  The mass extends from  slice 9 through 12  there is a clip in slice 11   A representative section of   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is submitted for tissue banking  Representative sections are submitted  A  radiograph accompanies a specimen demonstrating mass calcifications and clip  and a second mass with clip   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 1 with medial margin  perpendicular sections  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 2 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and medial and deep margins  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 2 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and deep and superior margins  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 2 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and anterior and superior margins  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 3 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and deep and inferior margins  2 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 3 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and anterior margin  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice 4 with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and anterior margin  1 frag 