Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 08 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer diagnosed by core biopsy  Evaluate margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION MEASURED FROM SLIDES  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  CYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND FOCAL MILD DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  4  FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  A few ducts with in situ carcinoma are present within the tumor mass  but not outside of it  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The resection margins are free of tumor  The gross intra operative diagnosis is confirmed  Stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   BIOPSY  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  BOTH SPECIMENS   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FIFTEEN OF FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left breast biopsy containing a 1 5cm tan firm lesion  1 0cm from the inked margin  A portion is given to Dr  Sgroi for research  A representative mass and closest margin  submitted in A through C  with surrounding representative sections in D through G  Labeled  A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm linear piece of fibrofatty tissue  entirely submitted in cassette H  Labeled  Left axillary contents  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary node dissection containing multiple pink to tan lymph nodes  The largest measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension  Submitted entirely in cassettes I through K  Labeled  Additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue containing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan to pink lymph node  entirely submitted in cassette L  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  APPROXIMATELY 1 CM FROM INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN PART C  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS PART D  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , 1st_Re-Excision.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 29 CLINICAL DATA  Status post biopsy   high grade infiltrating ductal carcinoma  No hormonal treatment  no radiation or chemotherapy  Now undergoing a left modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 03                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left breast and a separate fibrofatty axillary tissue designated  stitch at apex of axilla   measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The left breast has a skin ellipse  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm  a 3 8cm healed horizontal scar  4 0cm from the nipple  There is no orientation of the main specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal yellow  serous fluid and a biopsy cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  0 5cm inferior to the scar  The cavity is well defined with a firm  fibrous capsule  The biopsy cavity grossly abuts the closest deep inked margin in one area  Surrounding the biopsy cavity are focal areas of hemorrhage and indurated breast  areas of firm  white tissue with hemorrhagic foci  and cystic more yellow  gritty areas  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  The nipple is inverted and grossly unremarkable  The axillary nodes are as large as 1 4cm in diameter and are tan yellow  SEC