Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  25   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  Same Day Surgery Unit  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 08 43  Results To   Kevin S  Hughes MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT     Fibrotic breast parenchyma with focal stromal proliferation and perivascular  and periglandular chronic inflammation     Healing biopsy site     See note     NOTE  There is a focal stromal proliferation with associated abnormal collagen  that is present adjacent to the biopsy site  It appears consistent with an  alteration that existed prior to the development of the biopsy site scar  The  stromal proliferation has some features that are reminiscent of  pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  but overall  it is not typical for that  alteration  The association with periglandular and perivascular chronic  inflammation  which was also present in the core biopsy  raises some  consideration of autoimmune mastopathy  although the more characteristic  features of that process are absent  epithelioid myofibroblasts  lobular  atrophy   clinical correlation is suggested  No evidence of malignancy is  identified  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically  evaluated            Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD         CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast mass     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    left breast biopsy    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a short suture  designating anterior  a long suture designating lateral    a bowtie designated  cephalad  The long axis of the specimen runs from anterior to posterior  The  superior margin of the specimen is inked blue  the inferior margin black  the  medial margin green    the lateral margin yellow  The specimen contains  abundant dense white nodular fibrous tissue with moderate hemorrhage   a  spiral radiographic clip  as well as scant unremarkable fatty tissue  Entirely    sequentially submitted from anterior to posterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the clip  site as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID          PART   BREAST EXCISION  LEFT       report_end  , not_surgery.
