ered foci  ranging from   0 1cm to 0 2cm    and the  pattern is predominantly clinging with pleomorphic nuclei  A focus is present    0 1cm from the new black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Excision site changes are present   NOTE  The carcinoma in situ is unusual  It shows a predominantly solid growth  pattern with variable nuclear pleomorphism  Cribriforming architecture is  focally present   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    as is necrosis   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The presence of nuclear  pleomorphism  focal necrosis  and cribriforming are not typically seen in  classic LCIS and although some foci are consistent with LCIS  these findings  favor a diagnosis of CARCINOMA IN SITU with mixed ductal and lobular features   see prior excision specimens reviewed here    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Of note  some duct  profiles have cells with similar nuclear pleomorphism to the solid areas of  CIS  but instead have a clinging architectural pattern   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    For these  foci  CIS with mixed features cannot be excluded  Dr  S  Lester has also  reviewed the slides and agrees with the interpretation   CLINICAL DATA   History  Breast ca  Clinical Diagnosis   TISSUE SUBMITTED   Consult slides   appt  1 18  REMOVED_CASE_ID    GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received from Massachusetts General Hospital  Department of Pathology  Warren  II  Fruit Street  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  are twelve  12  H E stained slides labeled    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    sublabeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Level 1     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Level  2     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    corresponding  to A  breast  left  final medial margin  excision  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm    B  breast  left  final superior med