me  unit number   and  Left partial mastectomy short stitch superior long stitch lateral   and  consists of a partial mastectomy specimen including a small skin ellipse  2 1 x  0 6cm   present on the anterior surface and associated breast tissue measuring  4 2cm from the superior to inferior  2 3cm from medial to lateral  and 2 8cm  from the anterior to posterior  The specimen is inked according to protocol  for the evaluation of margins  red equals superior  green equals inferior   lateral equals yellow  medial equals orange  anterior equals blue  and  posterior equals black   The inking is based on two orienting sutures of which  the short suture designates the superior margin and the long suture represents  the lateral margin per surgeon  The specimen is serially sectioned from the  superior to inferior such that slice  1 is superior  The inferior most slice  is slice  8  In slices  3 through  5  there is a firm tan white focally  hemorrhagic ill defined nodule  just underneath the skin  The size of this  nodule is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The entire specimen is submitted for histologic  evaluation   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  3 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  2  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slices  3 5 including tumor nodule  1 frag per cassette   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  6  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  7  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  3 frags  ESS   ROH mmm  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  12 13  REMOVED_CASE_ID   SURGICAL ADDENDUM   Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE  1    Note  By report  the same results were obtained on the prior core needle  biopsy   Interpretation   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only  a portion of the membrane is positive   Positive  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10   of tumor cells   Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , Mastectomy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  ROS FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  55   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 9  BREAST ONC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 15 34  Results To   Jennifer S Temel MD  Thomas M Gudewicz MD    CLINICAL HISTORY   Breast Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for ROS    GROSS DESCRIPTION     1 block s  from Massachusetts General Hospital    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID             TEST    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Breast Adenocarcinoma    SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     FISH RESULTS   Fluorescence in situ hybridization of paraffin tumor tissue using a break apart  probe to the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus showed no rearrangement     ISCN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  nomenclature  nuc ish   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID x1 2  49 50     INTERPRETATION     NEGATIVE for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  rearrangement     TEST INFORMATION   Rearrangement involving the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene on chromosome 6q22 2 with one of several  putative partner genes  including  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5q32  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4p15 2   is present  in approximately 2  of lung adenocarcinomas  Lung tumors with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  rearrangement  have shown response to crizotinib in vitro   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  translocations generate  chimeric proteins containing a 5  end partner fused to the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  tyrosine kinase  domain at the 3  end  Deregulated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  activity has an oncogenic effect  and  targeted therapies against this kinase are currently being analyzed to treat  cancers harboring rearrangements in the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus     Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  using formalin fixed paraffin embedded  specimens has been shown to be an effective method for determining presence of  these translocations  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  break apart probe set targeting the 5  upstream region of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  the 3  downstream region of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   was hybridized  The number of  cells containing break apart signals or rearrangement is scored out of a total  50 cell count  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  rearrangement is reported if more than 15  of cells show  split signals  CPT codes for this test   REMOVED_CASE_ID   morphometric analysis  in situ  hybridization  each probe  manual  x 2     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA 88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Long Phi Le MD  PhD         PART   Molecular test for ROS       report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
