Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 54 CLINICAL DATA  IOG                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM   EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATICS AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE FINAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  CARCINOMA IN LYMPHATIC VESSELS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma and blood vessels is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  POSTERIOR INFERIOR  MARGIN    EXCISION  CARCINOMA IN LYMPHATIC VESSELS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma and blood vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISIONA  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 15 OF 20 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY LYMPHATIC VESSELS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Four specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  There is a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  blue is anterior  black is posterior  deep   superior is double inked in yellow  and inferior is double inked in green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fleshy white mass present at the deep margin and within 0 1cm of the anterior margin  SECTION CODE A  Deep  posterior  margin  B  Nearest margin  anterior   C G  Representative sections of mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   1  new anterior inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating the aspect furthest away from tumor which is inked in black  and the opposite aspect inked in blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue and has been submitted entirely in cassettes H through L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new posterior inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 