n normal or reactive conditions  It is rarely found in other  myeloproliferative disorders  We have developed a single base extension assay   SNaPshot  to genotype c  REMOVED_CASE_ID  in the forward and reverse directions from genomic  DNA samples from blood  bone marrow or splenectomies with extramedullary  hematopoiesis specimens  The analytic sensitivity of detecting the mutation has  been established in our laboratory at approximately 1  mutant allele frequency  or 2  heterozygous mutant cells     Baxter  E  J   L  M  Scott  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID    Acquired mutation of the tyrosine  kinase  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in human myeloproliferative disorders   Lancet 365  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_DATE  James  C   V  Ugo  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID    A unique clonal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation leading to  constitutive signaling causes polycythaemia vera   Nature 434  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_DATE  Kralovics  R   F  Passamonti  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID    A gain of function mutation of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   in myeloproliferative disorders   N Engl J Med 352 17   REMOVED_DATE  Levine  R  L   M  Wadleigh  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID    Activating mutation in the tyrosine  kinase  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in polycythemia vera  essential thrombocythemia  and myeloid  metaplasia with myelofibrosis   Cancer Cell 7 4   REMOVED_DATE  Zhao  R   S  Xing  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID    Identification of an acquired  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation in  polycythemia vera   J Biol Chem 280 24   REMOVED_DATE      This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these 