was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 13     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   Ten percent of the tumor cells stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  unlabeled  specimen confirmed with Dr  Ferguson via personal communication  consisting of two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  respectively  the former with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm diffusely tan white skin ellipse with a central red punctate depression  The specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous  slightly gritty breast tissue  A representative section from the larger portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  A representative section of the smaller portion is frozen as frozen section  2  and resubmitted in A  The remaining larger portion of breast tissue is submitted entirely in B through F  with the ends of the skin ellipse in B through C  and the smaller portion of breast tissue in G through I  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene 