ON_ID     Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   POSITIVE  3    NOTE  The patient presented with a right breast mass with peau d orange  appearance and erythema  On REMOVED_DATE  mammography showed a 2 4cm x 1 8cm  irregular mass at 12 00 with associated pleomorphic calcifications at the  medial and anterior spiculated margins of the mass  Extensive skin thickening  with fine linear calcifications were seen in the periareolar region  A core  needle biopsy showed a grade II III invasive ductal carcinoma  estrogen and  progesterone receptor negative and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu positive  3    BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    04 16 09   Fine needle aspiration of a right axillary lymph node was positive  for malignant cells  BC 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   04 16 09    After neoadjuvant therapy  per clinic note  08 12 09   physical exam showed  resolution of right breast fullness and peau d orange and markedly diminished  erythema   Gross examination of the specimen revealed a 3 0cm x 3 0cm x 2 0cm  ill defined fibrous area with clip located at 12 00 consistent with tumor bed   On corresponding slides tumor bed is present with multiple scattered foci of  DCIS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ve on immunostain performed  focal lymphovascular invasion within  the tumor bed  No residual invasive carcinoma is seen  Residual LVI is  additionally seen as scattered foci in nipple and skin dermal lymphatics and in  quadrants away from the tumor bed  The axillary contents were entirely  submitted for histological evaluation and it is difficult to identify  convincing residual encapsulated lymph node architecture following  chemotherapy  However foci of LVI are present  at least 8 discrete foci  mostly  in large vessels  up to 0 4cm   some with lymphoid aggregates around them  and  there is extensive tumor bed like fibrosis in adipose tissue suggestive of  prior metastatic carcinoma with extranodal extension  effectively treated by  chemotherapy  Miller Payne score is 5 since no residual invasive carcinoma is  present in the tumor bed  If foci of LVI in the axilla are counted as lymph  node metastases RCB is calculated at REMOVED_DATE  RCB II   AJCC Classification  6th edition   yp REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a     This case has been amended to correct a typographical error in the top line  breast laterality from left to right breast mastectomy  The diagnosis remains  unchanged   CLINICAL DATA   History  Hx of 5 cm Rt breast mass with changes suggestive of inflam CA     Rt  ax node  neo adj Herceptin   Taxol   Operation  Rt MRM   Operative Findings  See op node   Clinical Diagnosis  Rt breast mass with changes suggestive of inflam CA       TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  right breast  long suture lateral  short suture superior   B 2  right axillary dissection contents   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen was received in two pieces  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and MR  number   Part A  labeled  right breast long suture lateral short suture superior    consists of REMOVED_DATE grams simple mastectomy specimen measuring 16 5cm  superior  to inferior   8 5cm  medial to lateral   4 5cm  anterior to posterior   with  skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm  and an areolar complex of REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm   and everted nipple  1 2 x 1 2cm    The deep margin is intact and a smooth   bound by fascia  and inked black  Upon sectioning  the specimen reveals 80  of  adipose tissue and 20  of fibrous tissue with no palpable masses present  The  specimen is radiographed to identify the clip site which is located at 12 00   3 0cm from the nipple  The clip is surrounded by an ill defined soft fibrous  area  approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm    located 2 7cm from the deep resection  margin  The lateral breast tissue is carefully searched for lymph nodes but  none are found  The entire tumor bed and tissue from around it are submitted  along with represe