Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 36 CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications in upper outer quadrant  right breast   DCIS  Targeted calcifications in radiograph specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  Immunohistochemical staining for E cadherin and high molecular weight keratin were performed to confirm the diagnosis of lobular neoplasia but these cells were not present on the deeper sections cut for immunostaining  Dr  F  Koerner concurs with the diagnoses  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 23 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are multiple fragments of tan yellow tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  which are entirely submitted in cassettes A E  Gross Description by  TOYA HARRIS Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Holly E Atlas  M D  Helenanne D alessandro  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  CORE BIOPSY , Mastectomy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient  MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE  Path Subspecialty Service  Renal  Results To  OPEYEMI A OLABISI  M D  PH D   Resident  Lida Hariri  M D   Ph D   Signed Out by  R  Neal Smith  M D         CLINICAL DATA   49 y o Brazilian woman with a history of SLE   high titer speckled ANA   RNP     antiphospholipid Ab  class II GN  urticarial vasculitis   leucopenia  anemia   and Raynaud s  Cr   REMOVED_DATE PT  PTT wnl   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   63   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    14  neg cryo  TUP   REMOVED_DATE gms       FINAL DIAGNOSIS   KIDNEY  BIOPSY   LUPUS NEPHRITIS  CLASS II WITH IMMUNE COMPLEX INTERSTITIAL NEPHRITIS AND  SECONDARY  FOCAL AND SEGMENTAL GLOMERULOSCLEROSIS   ARTERIOSCLEROSIS     Note  All preparations of cortex and medulla contain about 16 glomeruli  of  which 5 are globally sclerotic  In the paraffin tissue of the remaining 9  non sclerotic two show mesangial expansion with mononuclear cells with an  adhesion  one shows mesangial hypercellularity  and 6 show mesangial  hypercellularity with segmental scars  Glomerular crescents and necrosis are  not identified  Endocapillary hypercellularity is not present  Pseudothrombi  are not identified  Podocytes are reactive  The basement membrane is slightly  thickened  The interstitium contains focal inflammatory infiltrate of mostly  mononuclear cells with tubulitis involving 10  of the cortical area  Fibrosis  and tubular atrophy affect about 35  of the cortical area  Some tubules are  hypertrophied  Many tubules contain Tamm Horsfall protein casts  Some tubules  contain prominent reabsorption droplets  Small arteries show intimal  hyperplasia or medial sclerosis  Focal arteriolar hyalinosis is not identified   Vasculitis or thrombi are not present     Immunofluorescence on frozen tissue with 2 glomeruli  none globally sclerotic   shows granular basement membrane staining for IgG  2 3    IgA  2    IgM  3      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3    kappa  2 3    and lambda  2 3   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID q  3    plus granular mesangial  staining of IgG  2 3    IgA  2    IgM  3 4     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3    kappa  2 3    lambda   3   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID q  3    The mesangial staining is global and diffuse  while the GBM  staining is focal and segmental  Some glomeruli show focal  segmental staining  of for fibrin  IgM and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   There is focal granular tubular basement membrane  staining for IgG  IgM  IgA  kappa  and lambda   plus focal granular  interstitial granular staining for IgG  IgM   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID q  fibrin  kappa  and lambda   Casts and tubular reabsorption droplets stain with multiple reactants  and  casts stain with similar intensity for both kappa and lambda     Digital images from the electron microscopy of renal tissue with three  glomeruli shows widespread granular mesangial deposits plus rare  intramembranous and subendothelial deposits  Although most deposits are  amorphous  some show a fibrillary fingerprint substructure  TBM deposits are  identified  A tubuloreticular structure is identified  Segmental foot process  effacement and duplication are present  The GBM is uniformly slightly  thickened without evidence of resorbed deposits or irregular contours     The present biopsy shows class II lupus nephritis and immune complex  interstitial nephritis plus focal segmental glomerulosclerosis and vascular  disease  Compared to the previous biopsy with class II lupus nephritis and  immune complex interstitial nephritis  the overall pattern is similar with the  exception of focal sclerosis  which was not present in the prior biopsy   Allowing for sampling error the degree of global glomerulosclerosis is not  increased  but the vascular disease may be worse  Although the extent of the  interstitial inflammation is comparable in the two biopsies  the tubular  atrophy and interstitial fibrosis have increased  suggesting that a component  of renal injury is the immune complex interstitial nephritis  No diagnostic  lesions of class III lupus nephritis were identified in either biopsy     These findings may be interpreted in two ways  If it is assumed that all  glomerular disease is lupus related  then because more than 50  of glomeruli  show global or segment scars  this would force a diagnosis of class IV chronic   not active  segmental and global sclerosing lupus nephritis plus immune  complex interstitial nephritis  This interpretation is not favored  Favored is  that some of the focal segmental and global sclerosis are related to nephron  loss  due to the uniformly slightly thickened GBM and hypertrophied tubules   and vascular disease  so that the diagnosis is class II lupus nephritis plus  immune complex interstitial nephritis with secondary focal segmental sclerosis  with the increased tubular atrophy and interstitial fibrosis attributed to the  activity of the immune complex interstitial nephritis     Reviewed for this case were multiple sections including H E  PAS  trichrome     toluidine blue  plus immunofluorescence slides stained for IgG  IgA  IgM   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID q  albumin  kappa  lambda    fibrin  plus digital images of electron  microscopy     Presented at renal pathology case consensus conference with Drs  E  E   Schneeberger  D  Taheri    R  B  Colvin     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  tan cylindrical soft tissue submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Final Diagnosis by R  Neal Smith M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH  25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 30 55PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART   Kidney  Left   Biopsy       report_end  , Mastectomy.
