Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  JULIE L JONES M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Ann K Folkins  M D   Pathologist  Jonathan N Glickman  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF  CALCIFICATIONS   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  clinging type  high nuclear grade  with apocrine  features  is present involving a complex sclerosing lesion in 5 of 7 blocks   see note    Calcifications are present associated with the complex sclerosing lesion  The  calcifications do not appear to be specifically associated with DCIS  No  necrosis is seen   The prior core needle biopsy site is present within the complex sclerosing  lesion   DCIS is   0 1cm from the inferior  medial  posterior  anterior  and lateral  margins  The superior margin is not well seen in the sections   Immunoperoxidase studies reveal that the majority of the DCIS is negative for  estrogen and progesterone receptors  Focal positivity cannot be excluded due  to the involvement of the sclerosing lesion  Some areas of the DCIS are  negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu and other areas show patchy moderate membrane  immunoreactivity   Note  This is an unusual form of DCIS  The degree of nuclear atypia  with  anaplastic appearing nuclei in some areas  and the presence of occasional  atypical mitotic figures  warrants a diagnosis of DCIS   This case was reviewed by Dr  Susan Lester and Dr  Deborah Dillon  who concur  with this interpretation   CLINICAL DATA   History  Left breast calcifications with severe atypia on core needle biopsy   Operation  Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy   Operative Findings  None given   Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast atypia on core biopsy   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast wire localized excision  short suture   superior  long  lateral