Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA DISPLAYING BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  GRADE 2  8 CM  EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 16 OF 16 LYMPH NODES AND EXTENDING INTO AXILLARY FAT  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   HIGHEST AXILLARY NODES    METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES AND EXTENDING INTO AXILLARY FAT  BREAST  LEFT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast biopsy  are two fragments of soft tissue  one is a fragment of breast REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The other is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse  The breast fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal mottled  white tan  fatty tissue  The skin fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm white  tan firm tissue beneath the epidermis  Representative sections from both fragments are frozen in FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the breast tissue is submitted entirely in cassette B  The remainder of the skin fragment are submitted entirely in cassettes C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 640 gram  20 x 15 x 4 2cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 20 x 15cm skin ellipse in front with a 3cm horizontal incision closed with sutures just medial to the nipple  Attached axillary tail measures 10 x 6 x 2 0cm  The entire specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm irregularly shaped white firm mass that grossly abuts against the posterior resection margin on the medial half of the specimen  SECTION CODE D  Tumor mass at posterior margin  medial half  E  Medial end of the tumor  F  Section taken from the middle of the tumor  G  Section of tumor at its lateral end  Thirteen lymph nodes of varying sizes are dissected from the axillary tail  The largest lymph node measures 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Seven medium sized lymph nodes  1 5cm to 2 0cm in length  and four smaller lymph nodes  0 5cm to 1 0cm in length  are identified  Each of these lymph nodes are bisected in half  and each half are submitted in cassettes H through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  highest chest wall node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue with a stitch on one end  noted on the requisition form as the highest axillary node in accessory tissue  dissection reveals three lymph nodes each approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Each node is bisected in half and the three halves are submitted in cassette N  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT   EXTENSIVE INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   HIGHEST    report_end  , not_surgery.
